sam (docs): Quick one — adding a compact "429s & timeouts" tip for the troubleshooting page. Need tiny py/js snippets, a short mitigation checklist, and a migration bullet about trim helpers. Can someone review?

mira (eng-runtime): TL;DR: honor Retry-After if present; otherwise exponential backoff + full jitter; cap at ~30s; after ~3 retries suggest failover to a lighter model. Call out KV-cache cold starts — first requests may timeout.

alex (devex): JS snippet (AbortController + retry):```js
async function apiRetry(url, opts = {}, retries = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= retries; i++) {
    const c = new AbortController();
    const t = setTimeout(() => c.abort(), opts.timeout || 60000);
    try {
      const r = await fetch(url, { ...opts, signal: c.signal });
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (r.status === 429) {
        const ra = r.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? Number(ra) : Math.min(Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random(), 30);
        await new Promise(s => setTimeout(s, wait * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      if (!r.ok) throw new Error('http error');
      return await r.json();
    } catch (e) {
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (e.name === 'AbortError' && i < retries) {
        await new Promise(s => setTimeout(s, (Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random()) * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
}
```

alex (devex): Python snippet (requests + jitter):```python
import time, random
import requests

def post_retry(url, payload, max_retries=3, timeout=60):
    for attempt in range(max_retries + 1):
        r = requests.post(url, json=payload, timeout=timeout)
        if r.status_code == 429:
            ra = r.headers.get('Retry-After')
            wait = int(ra) if ra and ra.isdigit() else min((2 ** attempt) + random.random(), 30)
            time.sleep(wait)
            continue
        r.raise_for_status()
        return r.json()
    raise RuntimeError('retries exhausted')
```

